# Qalam Monorepo — Core

Qalam is an education platform monorepo: .NET 8 backend at root, three frontends under `apps/`.

## Layout

| Path | Stack | Role |
|------|-------|------|
| `Qalam.Api/` | ASP.NET Core | HTTP API entry |
| `Qalam.Core/` | MediatR CQRS | Commands, queries, handlers |
| `Qalam.Service/` | .NET | Domain services |
| `Qalam.Data/` | .NET | Entities, DTOs, `Router.cs` |
| `Qalam.Infrastructure/` | EF Core | DbContext, migrations, seeders |
| `Qalam.MessagingApi/` | .NET | Email/SMS/push via RabbitMQ |
| `apps/admin/` | Next.js 16 | Admin web (submodule) |
| `apps/teacher/` | Vite + TanStack | Teacher web (submodule) |
| `apps/Qalam/` | Flutter | Student app |

## Principles

1. **Smallest correct diff** — no drive-by refactors across layers or apps.
2. **Backend: clean architecture + CQRS** — repositories, enhanced query projections, services.
3. **Mobile: Thkel architecture always** — see `apps/Qalam/.cursor/rules/thkel-architecture.mdc`.
4. **Business docs are authoritative** — `BUSINESS_LOGIC.md`, `docs/USER-STORIES-Scenarios-1-and-2.md`.
5. **Education domains use `code`** — never hardcode DB ids.

## Submodules

`apps/admin` and `apps/teacher` are git submodules with independent repos. Commit/push inside each app directory for frontend changes; bump submodule SHA in monorepo when integrating.

